    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "Anna, Bill, Cynthia, and Della have one pet each. The pets are a dog, a cat, a fish, and a hamster. Anna does not have the fish nor the dog. Bill does not have the dog nor the fish nor the hamster. Who has the hamster?",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "Anna"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "Bill"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "Cynthia"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "Della"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "Cannot be certain"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "A",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Start with Bill",
        "body": "Bill does not have the dog, the fish or the hamster, so Bill has the **cat**. Anna does not have the fish or the dog, and the cat belongs to Bill, so Anna has the **hamster**.\n\n**Answer: (A) Anna**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Use a table",
        "body": "Make a table with the children and the pets and cross out what is not allowed. Bill's row has only 'cat' left. Then in Anna's row, fish, dog and cat are crossed out, so Anna has the hamster. (Cynthia and Della have the dog and the fish, in some order — but that is not asked.)\n\n**Answer: (A) Anna**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
      "logic"
    ],
