    "prompt": "Two lighthouses blink at night to steer the boats safely into the harbour in the dark or in bad weather. One lighthouse flashes every five seconds, the other every seven seconds. How many seconds will elapse between the time the two lighthouses blink together and the next time it happens?",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "5"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "7"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "12"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "35"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "Never"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "D",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "List the flashes",
        "body": "After they blink together, the first lighthouse flashes after 5, 10, 15, 20, 25, 30, **35**, ... seconds and the second after 7, 14, 21, 28, **35**, ... seconds. The first time they match again is after 35 seconds.\n\n**Answer: (D) 35**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Common multiple",
        "body": "They blink together again after a number of seconds that is a multiple of both 5 and 7. The smallest such number is $5\\times 7 = 35$ (5 and 7 have no common factor).\n\n**Answer: (D) 35**"
      }
    ],
