    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "List the numbers",
        "body": "Two-digit numbers with digit sum 12: 39, 48, 57, 66, 75, 84, 93. Swap the digits and compare:\n\n- 39 → 93 (54 more)\n- 48 → 84 (36 more)\n- 57 → 75 (**18 more** ✔)\n- 66 → 66 (same)\n\nThe number is 57, and $5\\times 7 = 35$.\n\n**Answer: (C) 35**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Swapping digits",
        "body": "When the digits of a two-digit number are swapped, the number changes by 9 times the difference of the digits. A change of 18 means the digits differ by 2. Two digits with sum 12 and difference 2 are 5 and 7. Product $5\\times 7 = 35$.\n\n**Answer: (C) 35**"
      }
