      {
        "title": "Count how often each position was used",
        "body": "The $2\\times2$ shape fits in 7 positions. Some cells are covered by only one position, and they tell us how often that position was used:\n\n- top-left corner cell (3): the top position was used 3 times.\n- left cell of row 3 (2): the position below it was used 2 times.\n- right cell of row 2 (4): the position covering it was used 4 times.\n- bottom-left cell of row 5 (2): the lowest-left position, 2 times.\n- right cell of row 4 (1): the lowest-right position, 1 time.\n\nThe 6 in row 2 is covered by the top position (3), the position below it (2) and the middle position of rows 2–3 (so that one was used $6-3-2 = 1$ time). The 7 in row 4 is covered by the three positions around it: $7 - 2 - 1 = 4$ uses for the position covering rows 3–4.\n\nThe cell in row 3, column 3 is covered by three positions used 1, 4 and 4 times: $1 + 4 + 4 = 9$. The other hidden cells are 3, 5, 5, 3, 8, 6, 3 and 1, all smaller.\n\n**Answer: (D) 9**"
